{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwWYn3VTysF9FsjptrLZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I didn't check that the dashboard panels render, and the rule hasn't run yet (its status is still \"pending\").\n\n**What the data holds:** the sample logs have one document per web request. Key fields are `timestamp`, `response` (a string such as 200, 404 or 503), `bytes`, `extension`, `clientip`, `geo.src`/`geo.dest`, `machine.os`, `url` and `referer`. Most requests are 200s (12,832), with 801 404s and 441 503s.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-dd499103 Web logs overview\" (id `eff-dd499103-web-logs-overview-874a24dc6f97`) has four panels:\n- Total requests\n- Requests over time\n- Requests by response code\n- Average bytes by extension\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-dd499103 5xx spike\" (id `b75cf5ab-cc8d-4969-b652-dfae66cd76a1`) is an Elasticsearch query rule. It runs every minute over a 5-minute window and fires when more than 10 documents have a `response` of 500–599.\n\nThe rule has no actions attached, so it will show up as an alert in Kibana but won't send a notification anywhere."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":499,"cache_read_input_tokens":20812,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":499},"output_tokens":419,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"f7320a38-61e8-48bf-851a-3eb7fb4757aa","timestamp":"2026-10-12T01:55:02.036Z","request_id":"req_011CfwWYmncSQoFLipQeiFwB"}
